  "tables": {
    "source_ref": [
      {"id": "SR-6P10-TITLE", "source_document_id": "SD-MUTCD11-CH6-2023-12", "section": "6P.01", "paragraph": null, "table": null, "figure": "6P-10", "note": null,
       "page_printed": "878", "page_pdf": 114, "strength": "SUPPORT", "evidence": "QUOTE", "transcription": null, "figure_render": null,
       "quote": "Notes for Figure 6P-10—Typical Application 10 Lane Closure on a Two-Lane Road Using Flaggers"},
      {"id": "SR-6P10-FIG-TITLE", "source_document_id": "SD-MUTCD11-CH6-2023-12", "section": "6P.01", "paragraph": null, "table": null, "figure": "6P-10", "note": null,
       "page_printed": "879", "page_pdf": 115, "strength": "SUPPORT", "evidence": "QUOTE", "transcription": null, "figure_render": null,
       "quote": "Figure 6P-10. Lane Closure on a Two-Lane Road Using Flaggers (TA-10)"},
      {"id": "SR-6N09-TITLE", "source_document_id": "SD-MUTCD11-CH6-2023-12", "section": "6N.09", "paragraph": null, "table": null, "figure": null, "note": null,
       "page_printed": "846", "page_pdf": 82, "strength": "SUPPORT", "evidence": "QUOTE", "transcription": null, "figure_render": null,
       "quote": "Section 6N.09 Work within the Traveled Way of a Two-Lane Highway"},
      {"id": "SR-6N09-P07", "source_document_id": "SD-MUTCD11-CH6-2023-12", "section": "6N.09", "paragraph": "07", "table": null, "figure": "6P-10", "note": null,
       "page_printed": "846", "page_pdf": 82, "strength": "OPTION", "evidence": "QUOTE", "transcription": null, "figure_render": null,
       "quote": "Flaggers may be used as shown in Figure 6P-10."},
      {"id": "SR-6P10-N1", "source_document_id": "SD-MUTCD11-CH6-2023-12", "section": "6P.01", "paragraph": null, "table": null, "figure": "6P-10", "note": "1",
       "page_printed": "878", "page_pdf": 114, "strength": "OPTION", "evidence": "QUOTE", "transcription": null, "figure_render": null,
       "quote": "Positive protection devices may be used per Section 6M.02."},
      {"id": "SR-6P10-N2", "source_document_id": "SD-MUTCD11-CH6-2023-12", "section": "6P.01", "paragraph": null, "table": null, "figure": "6P-10", "note": "2",
       "page_printed": "878", "page_pdf": 114, "strength": "OPTION", "evidence": "QUOTE", "transcription": null, "figure_render": null,
       "quote": "For low-volume situations with short TTC zones on straight roadways where the flagger is visible to road users approaching from both directions, a single flagger, positioned to be visible to road users approaching from both directions, may be used (see Chapter 6D)."},
      {"id": "SR-6P10-N3", "source_document_id": "SD-MUTCD11-CH6-2023-12", "section": "6P.01", "paragraph": null, "table": null, "figure": "6P-10", "note": "3",
       "page_printed": "878", "page_pdf": 114, "strength": "OPTION", "evidence": "QUOTE", "transcription": null, "figure_render": null,
       "quote": "The ROAD WORK AHEAD and the END ROAD WORK signs may be omitted for short-duration operations."},
      {"id": "SR-6P10-N4", "source_document_id": "SD-MUTCD11-CH6-2023-12", "section": "6P.01", "paragraph": null, "table": null, "figure": "6P-10", "note": "4",
       "page_printed": "878", "page_pdf": 114, "strength": "OPTION", "evidence": "QUOTE", "transcription": null, "figure_render": null,
       "quote": "Flashing warning lights and/or flags may be used to call attention to the advance warning signs. A BE PREPARED TO STOP sign may be added to the sign series."},
      {"id": "SR-6P10-N5", "source_document_id": "SD-MUTCD11-CH6-2023-12", "section": "6P.01", "paragraph": null, "table": null, "figure": "6P-10", "note": "5",
       "page_printed": "878", "page_pdf": 114, "strength": "OPTION", "evidence": "QUOTE", "transcription": null, "figure_render": null,
       "quote": "Automated Flagger Assistance Devices (see Section 6L.02) may be used in situations where there is only one lane of approaching traffic in the direction to be controlled."},
      {"id": "SR-6P10-N6", "source_document_id": "SD-MUTCD11-CH6-2023-12", "section": "6P.01", "paragraph": null, "table": null, "figure": "6P-10", "note": "6",
       "page_printed": "878", "page_pdf": 114, "strength": "GUIDANCE", "evidence": "QUOTE", "transcription": null, "figure_render": null,
       "quote": "The buffer space should be extended so that the two-way traffic taper is placed before a horizontal (or crest vertical) curve to provide adequate sight distance for the flagger and a queue of stopped vehicles."},
      {"id": "SR-6P10-N7", "source_document_id": "SD-MUTCD11-CH6-2023-12", "section": "6P.01", "paragraph": null, "table": null, "figure": "6P-10", "note": "7",
       "page_printed": "878", "page_pdf": 114, "strength": "STANDARD", "evidence": "QUOTE", "transcription": null, "figure_render": null,
       "quote": "At night, flagger stations shall be illuminated, except in emergencies."},
      {"id": "SR-6P10-N8", "source_document_id": "SD-MUTCD11-CH6-2023-12", "section": "6P.01", "paragraph": null, "table": null, "figure": "6P-10", "note": "8",
       "page_printed": "878", "page_pdf": 114, "strength": "GUIDANCE", "evidence": "QUOTE", "transcription": null, "figure_render": null,
       "quote": "When used, the BE PREPARED TO STOP sign should be located between the Flagger sign and the ONE LANE ROAD sign."},
      {"id": "SR-6P10-N9", "source_document_id": "SD-MUTCD11-CH6-2023-12", "section": "6P.01", "paragraph": null, "table": null, "figure": "6P-10", "note": "9",
       "page_printed": "878", "page_pdf": 114, "strength": "GUIDANCE", "evidence": "QUOTE", "transcription": null, "figure_render": null,
       "quote": "When a grade crossing exists within or upstream of the transition area and it is anticipated that queues resulting from the lane closure might extend through the grade crossing, the TTC zone should be extended so that the transition area precedes the grade crossing."},
      {"id": "SR-6P10-N10", "source_document_id": "SD-MUTCD11-CH6-2023-12", "section": "6P.01", "paragraph": null, "table": null, "figure": "6P-10", "note": "10",
       "page_printed": "878", "page_pdf": 114, "strength": "GUIDANCE", "evidence": "QUOTE", "transcription": null, "figure_render": null,
       "quote": "When a grade crossing equipped with active warning devices exists within the activity area, provisions should be made for keeping flaggers informed as to the activation status of these warning devices."},
      {"id": "SR-6P10-N11", "source_document_id": "SD-MUTCD11-CH6-2023-12", "section": "6P.01", "paragraph": null, "table": null, "figure": "6P-10", "note": "11",
       "page_printed": "878", "page_pdf": 114, "strength": "GUIDANCE", "evidence": "QUOTE", "transcription": null, "figure_render": null,
       "quote": "When a grade crossing exists within the activity area, drivers operating on the left-hand side of the normal center line should be provided with comparable warning devices as for drivers operating on the right-hand side of the normal center line."},
      {"id": "SR-6P10-N12", "source_document_id": "SD-MUTCD11-CH6-2023-12", "section": "6P.01", "paragraph": null, "table": null, "figure": "6P-10", "note": "12",
       "page_printed": "878", "page_pdf": 114, "strength": "GUIDANCE", "evidence": "QUOTE", "transcription": null, "figure_render": null,
       "quote": "Early coordination with the railroad company or transit agency should occur before work starts."},
      {"id": "SR-6P10-N13", "source_document_id": "SD-MUTCD11-CH6-2023-12", "section": "6P.01", "paragraph": null, "table": null, "figure": "6P-10", "note": "13",
       "page_printed": "878", "page_pdf": 114, "strength": "OPTION", "evidence": "QUOTE", "transcription": null, "figure_render": null,
       "quote": "A flagger or a uniformed law enforcement officer may be used at the grade crossing to minimize the probability that vehicles are stopped within 15 feet of the grade crossing, measured from both sides of the outside rails."},
      {"id": "SR-6P10-FIG-SIGNS", "source_document_id": "SD-MUTCD11-CH6-2023-12", "section": "6P.01", "paragraph": null, "table": null, "figure": "6P-10", "note": null,
       "page_printed": "879", "page_pdf": 115, "strength": "GUIDANCE", "evidence": "FIGURE_TRANSCRIPTION", "quote": null,
       "transcription": "Figure 6P-10 shows both directions. On each approach, from the work outward: a W20-7 Flagger sign at dimension A from the flagger station, a W20-4 ONE LANE ROAD XX FT sign at B, and a W20-1 ROAD WORK XX FT sign at C, each on the right-hand roadside. A W16-2P XX FEET plaque is drawn below W20-7 on both approaches; it is labelled '(optional)' on the upper approach and carries no label on the lower approach. A G20-2 END ROAD WORK sign labelled '(optional)' stands at the end of each direction. A flagger stands at each end of the one-lane section.",
       "figure_render": {"uri": "tests/fixtures/rule_pack_sources/figures/figure_6P-10_p879.png", "sha256": "2cc22142fd8d86e7a2f338a5873894dfd5bf5530e938a296ddaf72cc62fe13d9", "size": 207421, "media_type": "image/png"}},
      {"id": "SR-6P10-FIG-TAPER", "source_document_id": "SD-MUTCD11-CH6-2023-12", "section": "6P.01", "paragraph": null, "table": null, "figure": "6P-10", "note": null,
       "page_printed": "879", "page_pdf": 115, "strength": "GUIDANCE", "evidence": "FIGURE_TRANSCRIPTION", "quote": null,
       "transcription": "Figure 6P-10: the one-lane, two-way taper of channelizing devices at each end of the work space is dimensioned '50 to 100 ft'.",
       "figure_render": {"uri": "tests/fixtures/rule_pack_sources/figures/figure_6P-10_p879.png", "sha256": "2cc22142fd8d86e7a2f338a5873894dfd5bf5530e938a296ddaf72cc62fe13d9", "size": 207421, "media_type": "image/png"}},
      {"id": "SR-6P10-FIG-ANCHOR", "source_document_id": "SD-MUTCD11-CH6-2023-12", "section": "6P.01", "paragraph": null, "table": null, "figure": "6P-10", "note": null, "page_printed": "879", "page_pdf": 115, "strength": "GUIDANCE", "evidence": "FIGURE_TRANSCRIPTION", "quote": null, "transcription": "Figure 6P-10, both approaches: C runs from the W20-1 sign support to the W20-4 support, B from the W20-4 support to the W20-7 support, and A from the W20-7 support to a line level with the flagger. The one-lane, two-way taper ('50 to 100 ft') starts at that line and runs toward the work space. C, B and A are consecutive and do not overlap.", "figure_render": {"uri": "tests/fixtures/rule_pack_sources/figures/figure_6P-10_p879.png", "sha256": "2cc22142fd8d86e7a2f338a5873894dfd5bf5530e938a296ddaf72cc62fe13d9", "size": 207421, "media_type": "image/png"}}
    ],
